6. One-Slide Interview Summary 💡
In a Snowflake project, Snowpipe handles continuous ingestion into raw tables, Streams track incremental changes, and Tasks transform data into curated tables. Schemas are used to logically separate ingestion, CDC, and orchestration layers.


==========Snowflake End-to-End Flow==============

Snowpipe + Streams + Tasks (with Examples)
Use Case
Load files continuously from cloud storage → process incremental changes → populate curated tables automatically.
________________________________________
High-Level Architecture
Cloud Storage (S3 / ADLS / GCS)
        ↓
External Stage
        ↓
Snowpipe (Auto Ingest)
        ↓
Raw Table
        ↓
Stream (CDC)
        ↓
Task
        ↓
Processed / Target Table

________________________________________
Components Involved (Interview Must-Know)
1.	Cloud Storage (S3 / ADLS / GCS)
2.	Storage Integration
3.	File Format
4.	External Stage
5.	Snowpipe
6.	Raw Table
7.	Stream
8.	Task
9.	Warehouse / Serverless Compute
________________________________________
Step 1: Create File Format
CREATE OR REPLACE FILE FORMAT csv_ff
TYPE = 'CSV'
FIELD_OPTIONALLY_ENCLOSED_BY = '"'
SKIP_HEADER = 1;
________________________________________
Step 2: Create Storage Integration
CREATE OR REPLACE STORAGE INTEGRATION s3_int
TYPE = EXTERNAL_STAGE
STORAGE_PROVIDER = S3
ENABLED = TRUE
STORAGE_AWS_ROLE_ARN = 'arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/snowflake_role'
STORAGE_ALLOWED_LOCATIONS = ('s3://sales-data-bucket/');
________________________________________
Step 3: Create External Stage
CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE sales_stage
URL = 's3://sales-data-bucket/orders/'
STORAGE_INTEGRATION = s3_int
FILE_FORMAT = csv_ff;
________________________________________
Step 4: Create Raw Table
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE orders_raw (
    order_id INT,
    customer_id INT,
    amount NUMBER(10,2),
    status STRING,
    load_ts TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);
________________________________________
Step 5: Create Snowpipe
CREATE OR REPLACE PIPE orders_pipe
AUTO_INGEST = TRUE
AS
COPY INTO orders_raw
FROM @sales_stage
FILE_FORMAT = csv_ff;

What Snowpipe Does
•	Automatically loads new files
•	Uses serverless compute
•	No warehouse required
________________________________________
Step 6: Cloud Notification (AWS Example)
•	S3 Event → SNS → SQS → Snowpipe
•	Enables auto-ingest
📌 Interview line:
Snowpipe uses event notifications, not polling.
________________________________________
Step 7: Create Stream on Raw Table
CREATE OR REPLACE STREAM orders_raw_stream
ON TABLE orders_raw;
Stream Captures
•	INSERTs from Snowpipe loads
•	Metadata columns:
o	METADATA$ACTION
o	METADATA$ISUPDATE
________________________________________
Step 8: Create Target (Processed) Table
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE orders_curated (
    order_id INT,
    customer_id INT,
    amount NUMBER(10,2),
    status STRING,
    last_updated TIMESTAMP
);
________________________________________
Step 9: Create Task to Process Stream
CREATE OR REPLACE TASK process_orders_task
WAREHOUSE = etl_wh
SCHEDULE = '5 minutes'
WHEN SYSTEM$STREAM_HAS_DATA('orders_raw_stream')
AS
MERGE INTO orders_curated t
USING orders_raw_stream s
ON t.order_id = s.order_id

WHEN MATCHED THEN
    UPDATE SET
        t.customer_id = s.customer_id,
        t.amount = s.amount,
        t.status = s.status,
        t.last_updated = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP

WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN
    INSERT (order_id, customer_id, amount, status, last_updated)
    VALUES (
        s.order_id,
        s.customer_id,
        s.amount,
        s.status,
        CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
    );
________________________________________
Step 10: Start the Task
ALTER TASK process_orders_task RESUME;
________________________________________
End-to-End Data Flow (Step by Step)
1.	File lands in S3
2.	Event triggers Snowpipe
3.	Snowpipe loads data into orders_raw
4.	Stream captures incremental rows
5.	Task detects stream data
6.	Task processes data into orders_curated
7.	Stream offset advances (exactly once)
________________________________________
Key Differences: Snowpipe vs Task
Feature	Snowpipe	Task
Purpose	Load files	Transform data
Compute	Serverless	Warehouse / Serverless
Trigger	Storage event	Schedule / Condition
CDC	❌	✔ via Streams
________________________________________
Failure Handling (Production Scenario)
If Snowpipe fails
•	File stays unprocessed
•	Can be reloaded manually
If Task fails
•	Stream data is preserved
•	Fix issue → rerun task
________________________________________
Common Interview Questions & Answers
Q: Can Snowpipe directly load into target tables?
✔ Yes, but best practice is raw → stream → task → curated.
Q: Can tasks consume Snowpipe directly?
❌ No, tasks work on tables/streams.
Q: Does Snowpipe support updates/deletes?
❌ No, only INSERTs.
________________________________________
One-Line Interview Power Answer 💡
Snowpipe handles continuous file ingestion using serverless compute, Streams capture incremental changes on raw tables, and Tasks process those changes into curated tables, forming a fully automated end-to-end data pipeline in Snowflake.


